Playing a randomly generated lawful human valkyrie... didn't really
want to, but that was what the RNG coughed up.  This has been a trying
game, not so much that it has been hard, just fraught with a lack of
useful items.  Sokoban had an amulet of reflection, never saw a (BoH
until I wished for one with my first castle wand wish (which, by the
way, the wand was (0:1)... D'OH!). On the other hand, sacrificing has
garnered me Mjollnir, Grayswandir, and Frosty in that order, and of
course, being a lawful valk, I got Excalibur early on.  Also, I found
a +5 dagger in the gnomish mines that I occassionally use for
two-weaponing with Excalibur or Grayswandir.

After 18k turns, I finally hit XL 13, at which point I ran to my stash
in Sokoban, quaffed my 1 !oGL and did the quest.  Remarkably easy, as
usual.  None of the giants in Lord Surtur's lair had a /oStriking, so
that instadeath was out of the way.

It took almost 23k turns to get poison resistance (random tin of white
unicorn meat), then no more than 100 more turns to get telepathy
(killed at least a dozen floating eyes before with no corpses).  I got
to Medusa on level 21 (the shallowest it can be, right?) with the
titan, who was peaceful since Random is lawful.  I dug down, hoping
that Perseus' statue would have [BoLev.  It did.  It was only after I
cleared the castle that a cross-aligned unicorn was created giving me
its horn (over 30k turns now).

As I'm sitting in the VotD, getting ready for the plunge into
Gehennom, I decide to start wasting (MM charges on fixing up my rusty,
corroded, burnt armor.  Write a scroll of enchant armor, please.

b - blessed scroll labeled PRATYAVAYAH.

Oh, right... haven't seen any scrolls of that up til now either.  Hey,
I got that to work, even with the 30-odd% chance of success... And all
but one ?oEW have been self made, too.  This game has had the
streakiest, flukiest luck I've had in nethack for quite some time.

Other oddities:  I've seen no less than 20 suits of elven armor so
far.  It seems like 80% of the elves and 50% of the hobbits I've slain
have been well-kitted (including one elf with a blessed +3 suit). 
OTOH, I found only 1 suit of dwarven mithril, that in the maze one
level above the Castle.

I saw no dragons until I hit the castle, which is rather unusual for
as slow as this game has gone.  Finally got shock resistance from one
of the castle dragons.

The only useful rings I've found up through the castle were
invisibility and see invisible, which were made redundant the first
time I ate a stalker corpse.  I found 2 rings of levitation in the
VotD, allowing me to ditch Perseus' boots to save on weight.  I did
find an uncursed -1 ring of increase damage on the last level of the
quest...  Maybe I should head back there with a few ?oCharging...

